s always valid, there are no more dangling ends. If you add a new step, for example, an approval form, all output paths are connected. You do not have to connect, for example, the Reject outcome to the process anymore.      See Create and Configure Forms in a Vertical Layout Process Editor.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-01-22\nValid as Of: 2024-01-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3632 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Administrative Data in the Documentation Template\nDescription: You can now select whether you want to display the administrative data of your MIG and MAG in the documentation template.  See: MIGs and MAGs\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3633 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Display xsd:nillable value in a MIG\nDescription: You can now view if an element/node in a MIG allows nil values through the Nillable field.  See: Working with a Node\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3634 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Integration Advisor: 1.82.*    Increment: 2312    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-20\nValid as Of: 2024-01-20\nVersion: 2312\n\n--- Record 3635 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Support of xsd:nillable in Custom Messages\nDescription: Custom Messages now support xsd:nillable.  See: Custom Type Systems\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLi